                {
                    "id": "0be74e2f-9afb-46f8-ba6b-3bbc7f5d5016",
                    "notes": "This is is **SO** strong, stronger than Boost Recycler so long as you can actually swing. \n\nI don't know why it's in the weapon tab, it isn't in any of the default builds and is a hidden gem IMO. The build revolves around this, taking it early is definitely viable.",
                    "action": "optional",
                    "upgrade_id": "451f8c81-1821-48a4-a980-ae1cebd61a85"
                },
                {
                    "id": "c9c1c8fa-f71c-4861-a399-417011b92e5e",
                    "notes": "Great item. Make your armour 10% stronger until the enemy team are giga-spec'd into AP, making this more like a 50 extra health item (25 armour, 25 EHP) whist reducing enemy economy.",
                    "action": "buy",
                    "upgrade_id": "b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09"
                },
                {
                    "id": "e7e0f2d2-e874-4101-a20d-43c88815fbb7",
                    "notes": "This can be skipped, but it is really good value and is deceptive as it's an offensive item in this build. Shield Stampede makes your entire shield a hitbox for dealing the 'boop' damage (not the pin stun). Having a bigger shield makes it hit more stuff. Low hp enemies hiding round corners, flying characters. This also makes denying a floating mercy rez easier.\n\nMore shield health and personal health doesn't hurt.",
                    "action": "buy",
                    "upgrade_id": "e82af99e-3116-4867-b8a4-52c7dfd1d7e9"
                },
                {
                    "id": "2a67a55a-b307-4f65-b77f-9101ad1b9e4e",
                    "notes": "Use this to see when a squishy is waiting for heals in cover. Use your pin to pin PAST and have your shield kill them.",
                    "action": "buy",
                    "upgrade_id": "2a4ffaf4-f14b-47d2-a267-0a0e83e87418"
